// The default product type this template is geared toward
:videoType: YouTube explainer video
// The core topic, as supplied by the producer
:coreTopic: Image and restore my system disk with CloneZilla Live, with the system-and-data separation that makes destructive recovery safe
// The source material, as supplied by the producer
:sourceMaterial: The CloneZilla Live documentation (https://clonezilla.org/clonezilla-live-doc.php), specifically the "Save disk image" and "Restore disk image" step-by-step docs, plus the producer's real-world setup: a system disk kept separate from a 4-drive NAS (4 x 6TB in RAID-5 = 18TB usable) with a 5TB external USB drive backing the NAS up on a schedule
// The single most important sentence of the video: the core promise.
// It should be crystal clear, compelling, outcome-focused, and bolded
// wherever it is delivered.
:corePromise: I separate my system from my data. So when a new install bricks my system, my recovery is destructive: I wipe the drive, restore my disk image with CloneZilla, and I am back at a tested, known, stable state
// The default framework. Storytelling is best suited to explainer videos.
:framework: Storytelling
